      "preview": "יְבוּסִי: jebuseus e Jerusalém; gentílico e lugar.",
      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">יְבוּסִי</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">יְבֻסִי</span></big> <strong>1.</strong>  <strong> adjetivo gentílico: jebuseu, jebuseus</strong>; singular <span dir=\"rtl\">אורנה הַיְבֻסִי</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:16\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.16\">2 S 24:16</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:18\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.18\">18</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 21:15\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.21.15\">1 Ch 21:15</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 21:18\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.21.18\">18</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 21:28\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.21.28\">28</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 3:1\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.3.1\">2 Ch 3:1</a>; como substantivo, <em>um jebuseu</em> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 9:7\" href=\"/Zechariah.9.7\">Zc 9:7</a>; geralmente com artigo <span dir=\"rtl\">הַי׳</span> coletivamente: <em>os jebuseus</em>, em registro histórico <a data-ref=\"Genesis 10:16\" href=\"/Genesis.10.16\">Gn 10:16</a> (J) = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 1:14\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.1.14\">1 Ch 1:14</a> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:29\" href=\"/Numbers.13.29\">Nu 13:29</a> (E) <a data-ref=\"Joshua 9:1\" href=\"/Joshua.9.1\">Jos 9:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 11:3\" href=\"/Joshua.11.3\">11:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 12:8\" href=\"/Joshua.12.8\">12:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 24:11\" href=\"/Joshua.24.11\">24:11</a> (todos D) <a data-ref=\"Judges 3:5\" href=\"/Judges.3.5\">Ju 3:5</a> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 9:8\" href=\"/Nehemiah.9.8\">Ne 9:8</a>, todos em listas de povos cananeus; assim também <a data-ref=\"I Kings 9:20\" href=\"/I_Kings.9.20\">1 K 9:20</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 8:7\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.8.7\">2 Ch 8:7</a>, em que se menciona o remanescente desses povos; também <a data-ref=\"Ezra 9:1\" href=\"/Ezra.9.1\">Ezr 9:1</a>, o que parece mostrar que essa lista se tornara uma expressão estabelecida para os habitantes antigos; cf. ainda nas promessas (JED) <a data-ref=\"Genesis 15:21\" href=\"/Genesis.15.21\">Gn 15:21</a> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 3:8\" href=\"/Exodus.3.8\">Ex 3:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 3:17\" href=\"/Exodus.3.17\">17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 13:5\" href=\"/Exodus.13.5\">13:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 23:23\" href=\"/Exodus.23.23\">23:23</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 33:2\" href=\"/Exodus.33.2\">33:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 34:11\" href=\"/Exodus.34.11\">34:11</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 7:1\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.7.1\">Dt 7:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 20:17\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.20.17\">20:17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 3:10\" href=\"/Joshua.3.10\">Jos 3:10</a>; definidos especificamente como habitantes de Jebus-Jerusalém <a data-ref=\"Joshua 15:63\" href=\"/Joshua.15.63\">Jos 15:63</a><sup>(×2)</sup> (J) <a data-ref=\"Judges 1:21\" href=\"/Judges.1.21\">Ju 1:21</a><sup>(×2)</sup> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 5:6\" href=\"/II_Samuel.5.6\">2 S 5:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 5:8\" href=\"/II_Samuel.5.8\">8</a> (sobre esse trecho, cf. Dr) <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:6\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.6\">1 Ch 11:6</a> (chamados também <span dir=\"rtl\">יוֹשֵׁב הָאָרֶץ</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 5:6\" href=\"/II_Samuel.5.6\">2 S 5:6</a> & <span dir=\"rtl\">ישְׁבֵי הָאָרֶץ</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:4\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.4\">1 Ch 11:4</a>); veja-se também <span dir=\"rtl\">עִיר הַיְבוּסִי הַזֹּאת</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 19:11\" href=\"/Judges.19.11\">Ju 19:11</a>; daí<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>Jerusalém</em>, no Hexateuco somente em P, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 15:8\" href=\"/Joshua.15.8\">Jos 15:8</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">גֵּי בֶן־הִנֹּם אֶל־כֶּתֶף היבוסי מִנֶּגֶב הִיא יְרוּשָׁלָ֑םִ</span>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Joshua 18:16\" href=\"/Joshua.18.16\">18:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 18:28\" href=\"/Joshua.18.28\">18:28</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">וְהַיְבוּסִי הִיא יְרוּשָׁלַםִ</span>.—Cf. <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, כְּנַ֫עַן\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_כְּנַ֫עַן\">כנען</a>.",
